{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ethologic-antisolar-queenbee","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic `87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b` removed the default-reviewer mechanism entirely. Verified on\n`origin/main` at `5f618b3ccff`:\n\n- No reviewer prompt carries a `default:` front-matter key (`git grep -n \"^default:\" -- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` prints nothing).\n- `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py` has no default-reviewer logic; `select_reviewers`\n  at `:607` is purely `applies_to`-glob driven and returns `[]` for an empty change set.\n- The index invariant test (`test_index_has_exactly_one_default`) no longer exists.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` has 5 reviewers, none with a `default` key.\n\n`docs/release-notes.md` records the decision in both halves: the \"exactly one\n`default: true` reviewer\" index invariant is removed, and `select_reviewers([])` now\nreturns `[]` where it previously returned `['ticket-quality']`.\n\n**`docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md` was not updated and still documents the removed\nmechanism in two places:**\n\n- `:42` — a front-matter key table row:\n  `| `default`        | Whether this reviewer is in the default set (exactly one default; see §4). |`\n- `:201` — a stated authoring invariant: `**exactly one `default`** across reviewers`,\n  presented alongside the `dimension` rule as a validation violation.\n\nAn author following this file would add a `default:` key that the index builder no longer\nreads, and would expect a one-default check that no longer runs.\n\nThis residue was not caught by `a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711`'s AC1, whose grep pattern covers\n`_review_ticket_impl`, `review_workflows`, `ticket-quality`, `ticket_quality`,\n`rebar-ticket-quality` and `aggregate_findings` — it never searches for `default`.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Delete the `default` row from the front-matter key table at `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md:42`.\n2. Rewrite the invariant at `:201` so it states only the surviving cross-reviewer rule.\n   Read the surrounding sentence first and keep the `dimension` clause intact — the\n   `default` clause is one of two joined in that sentence, so this is an edit, not a\n   line deletion.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only. No code path changes, so the existing suite is unaffected; the\ncriteria below assert the on-disk text directly.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'exactly one default' docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md)\" -eq 0 ]` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC2** `[ \"$(grep -cF 'exactly one `default`' docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md)\" -eq 0 ]` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC3** `[ \"$(grep -c '^| `default`' docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md)\" -eq 0 ]` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC4** The `dimension` rule surviving at the former `:201` sentence is still\n      present: `grep -F 'no `dimension`' docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md` prints a line.\n- [ ] **AC5** `git grep -n \"^default:\" -- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` still prints nothing,\n      confirming the docs now match the code rather than the code having regressed.\n- [ ] **AC6** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly one path,\n      `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md`.\n- [ ] **AC7** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- **`docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md:114`, `:126-129`, `:251`, `:256`** all use the word\n  \"default\" for model selection and the `execution_mode` enum. Unrelated to reviewer\n  selection; they stay.\n- **Re-introducing a default reviewer.** The removal is a shipped, documented decision in\n  `docs/release-notes.md`; this ticket aligns the authoring guide with it and does not\n  revisit it.\n- **`a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711`'s AC3 and AC4**, which assert the pre-removal behavior and are\n  superseded by that decision. Their disposition is tracked on that ticket, not here.","id":"34ec-cd4e-5673-423a","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","docs-drift"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Authoring guide still documents the removed default-reviewer mechanism"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793383287768235539,"uuid":"62cb39ce-aae7-4e3d-91c7-f971cf6ca220"}